# Pinned sha256 for the lbug vector/fts extension binaries staged by
# scripts/stage-lbug-extensions.sh (issue #593, ADR-0593).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# extension.ladybugdb.com publishes extensions at a per-minor path
# (v<LBUG_EXTENSION_VERSION>/<platform>/<name>/) and overwrites the files at that path on
# patch releases — LBUG_EXTENSION_VERSION resolves to one shared directory for every 0.20.x
# core, so the bytes a build picks up depend on *when* it runs, not on anything pinned in this
# repository. This file pins the exact bytes stage-lbug-extensions.sh must receive; any other
# bytes fail the build instead of being silently staged. See ADR-0593 for the full design,
# including why a version-string diagnostic on mismatch is informational only, never a
# pass/fail signal — version equality is not the same as ABI compatibility.
#
# THIS FILE IS UPDATED BY HAND ONLY, after a human re-verifies new CDN bytes are safe to ship
# (e.g. via loop testing against the pinned core, as documented in issue #593's discussion).
# stage-lbug-extensions.sh never writes to this file.
#
# Format: one entry per line, "<platform> <extension> <sha256>", where <platform> is one of
# is vector or fts. Values below are the lbug 0.21.0 extensions (CDN path v0.21.0), fetched
# 2026-09-29 after upstream's 00:03 UTC republish (origin and edge agreed). Verified against an
